[b]Disclaimer: this mod was made with AI assistance.[/b] If you're not comfortable with that, please stop reading here.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Salvage/images/banner.jpg?v=2[/img]

Real salvaged parts for [b]Build 42[/b]: motors, compressors, heating elements, alternators, copper wire and more, each with its own condition. Part of the Dazed suite.

Version 0.1.0 is the first stage. The parts exist, turn up as loot and can be stripped from wire and generators. Stripping fridges, washers, other appliances and cars is not in yet.

[table]
[tr][td][b]Game version[/b][/td][td]Build 42 only (42.0+)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Requires[/b][/td][td][b]Dazed Core[/b] 1.7.0 or later (subscribe to it too)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Multiplayer[/b][/td][td]Yes. The server and every player need it[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Add mid-save[/b][/td][td]Yes. New loot only appears in containers that haven't been opened yet[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Mod ID[/b][/td][td]DazedSalvage[/td][/tr]
[/table]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Salvage/images/h-parts.png?v=2[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Salvage/images/parts.png?v=2[/img]
[list]
[*]Twenty items: small and large electric motors, a refrigeration compressor, copper tubing, a condenser coil, a fan motor, a thermostat, a heating element, a microwave transformer, a circuit board, a timer switch, a drive belt, a steel pressure tank, a small petrol engine, a pull starter, a coin mechanism, an alternator, a starter motor, a wiring harness and copper wire.
[*]Each part has its own condition.
[*]Icons are vanilla stand-ins for now.
[*]Every part carries a shared Dazed Core tag, so other Dazed mods can use salvaged parts in their recipes without requiring this one.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Salvage/images/h-strip.png?v=2[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Salvage/images/strip.png?v=2[/img]
[list]
[*][b]Strip Wire for Copper:[/b] 5 electric wire and a knife or pliers give 1 copper wire.
[*][b]Strip Generator for Parts:[/b] a vanilla generator and a screwdriver give a small engine, a pull starter, an alternator, copper wire and 2 sheet metal.
[*]Copper wire, copper tubing, condenser coils and coin mechanisms saw into vanilla copper scrap with vanilla's own recipes, so they feed Build 42 metalworking.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Salvage/images/h-loot.png?v=2[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Salvage/images/loot.png?v=2[/img]
[list]
[*]Loose parts in garages, mechanic shelves, generator rooms, electronics crates, electrician tools, junk piles and appliance stores. Shop parts are new; the rest are worn.
[*]Extra copper scrap, copper sheet, copper wire and copper tubing in metalworking, construction, electrical and plumbing loot.
[/list]

[h2]Planned[/h2]
[list]
[*]Strip fridges, freezers, washers, dryers, ovens, microwaves, AC units, TVs, computers, vending and arcade machines for parts.
[*]Recipes in Dazed Power, Dazed Plumbing and the Electric Vehicles add-on that use these parts.
[*]Take the alternator, starter motor and wiring harness out of cars.
[*]A winch for dragging wrecks off the road.
[/list]

[h2]Sandbox[/h2]
Two options on the Dazed Salvage page: how often salvaged parts turn up in loot, and how much extra copper is added. Set either to 0 to turn it off.

